cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "WebFixBench: a reproducible benchmark for LLM-assisted code review on web-application changes"
message: "If you use WebFixBench, please cite it as below, and state which suite version and prompt version you ran."
type: software
version: 0.1.0
date-released: "2026-09-20"
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/alexsinyaev/webfixbench"
abstract: >-
  WebFixBench is a reproducible benchmark for evaluating the reliability of
  LLM-assisted code review on web-application changes. Version 0.1 is an early
  research skeleton: an evaluation harness plus one suite, php-web-v0.1, of
  twelve labelled synthetic diffs covering PHP, Laravel and WordPress, including
  three clean controls that must produce no findings. It measures detection,
  false positives, malformed output and reported confidence. No model results
  are published in this version.
keywords:
  - benchmark
  - code review
  - large language models
  - evaluation
  - reliability
  - false positives
  - php
